.TH SUPER8IFY 1 "November 2026" "polajuice @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
super8ify \- phone clip in, 1970s Super 8 reel with magnetic-stripe sound out
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B super8ify
.I INPUT.MOV
.RI [ OUTPUT.mp4 ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B super8ify
turns a clip into a home movie: the picture goes through
.BR superjuice (1)
at 18 frames per second and 720 lines on the camera's canonical stock,
aged a little; the sound goes through
.BR audiotard (1)
(a tape chain, the bandwidth of a projector speaker, a small tube amp);
.BR ffmpeg (1)
marries them. The default output is
.IR INPUT_CAMERA.mp4
next to the input.
.PP
Everything is tuned through environment variables, defaults in
brackets. Only the ones set are passed on, so the camera's own defaults
hold otherwise.
.SS Picture
.TP
.B CAMERA
[super8] polajuice camera.
.TP
.B FILM
[the camera's canonical stock] film stock;
.B none
forces the scalar engine.
.TP
.B AGE
[0.25] 0 fresh .. 1 attic.
.TP
.B SEED
[7] grain seed.
.TP
.B FPS
[18] Super 8 ran at 18.
.TP
.B HEIGHT
[720] proxy height; real Super 8 resolved less.
.TP
.B FILTER
[] lens contrast filter (yellow, orange, red, green, blue).
.TP
.B GRAIN
[classic] classic or silver.
.TP
.B EDGE
[0] development edge effects 0..2.
.TP
.B RECIPE
[] a recipe file or polajuice JPEG to take the look from; the other
knobs apply on top.
.TP
.B EV, HALATION, DEVELOP, CROP
[0] [1] [normal] [camera] as polajuice's
.BR \-\-ev ", " \-\-halation ", " \-\-develop ", " \-\-crop .
.TP
.B TEMP TINT BLACK SHADOWS HIGHLIGHTS CONTRAST GRAD GRADANGLE GRADPOS
.TQ
.B DENOISE DISTORTION DEVIGNETTE ROTATE TRIMX TRIMY TRIMW TRIMH
[0] scene, lens and framing, as polajuice's
.BR \-\-temp " etc."
.TP
.B MOTION
[1] gate weave / flicker scale: 0.5 steadier, 2 a worn projector, 0
tripod-locked.
.SS Sound
.TP
.B SOUND
[stripe]
.B stripe
= the audiotard tape mangle;
.B clean
= the original audio untouched;
.B silent
= no audio (period-correct).
.TP
.B WOW, FLUTTER
[14] [10] speed wobble depth in cents, slow and fast.
.TP
.B HISS
[\-38] tape hiss in dBFS.
.TP
.B DRIVE, SHAPE
[2] [tube] tube drive into the small amp and its curve.
.TP
.B BAND
[120:5000] projector-speaker bandwidth lo:hi Hz.
.TP
.B AT_EXTRA
[] extra audiotard arguments verbatim, e.g.
.B AT_EXTRA="\-\-vinyl"
for the wrong era.
.SS Tools
.TP
.B SUPERJUICE, AUDIOTARD
Paths to the binaries when they are not on the PATH.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
    super8ify holiday.MOV
    CAMERA=bw\-35 FILTER=orange AGE=0.5 super8ify holiday.MOV noir.mp4
    FILM=kodak_kodachrome_64 SOUND=silent super8ify holiday.MOV
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR superjuice (1),
.BR polajuice (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1).
